libpkgapply-exec(7)

# NAME

libpkgapply-exec - exact package lifecycle execution adapter

# DESCRIPTION

*libpkgapply-exec* derives exact lifecycle nodes from one sealed
*libpkgapply* application request and executes one caller-selected node through
an injected *libpkgexec* backend.

Incoming installation nodes come from the exact source snapshot retained by the
incoming build. Installed removal nodes come only from durable historical
control in the accepted plan. Historically unavailable control is refused.

The returned node vector is canonical identity order and is not a transaction
schedule. The caller owns ordering relative to application, publication, other
nodes, and failure continuation.

# EXECUTION VIEW

The caller supplies an execution root containing the interpreter, exact native
numeric credentials, and a separate managed target root. The target is mounted writable at */target*. Networking is
denied, stdin is closed, stdout and stderr are captured completely, and the
environment is closed.

Version 0.1 executes only *text/x-posix-shell* lifecycle material, applies no
resource limits, and disables cancellation.

# EXCLUSIONS

The library does not apply filesystem plans, publish installed state, acquire
the outer target lease, resolve dependencies, choose transaction order, or
construct a Linux backend.

# SEE ALSO

*libpkgapply*(3), *libpkgexec*(3), *pkgexec_request*(3)
